text:
### Stand up for the freedom to fly: Rally at Alaska Airlines HQ this Tuesday 11/24!

Join Unions and community members at [Angle Lake Park](https://www.mapquest.com/directions/to/us/washington/angle-lake-park-346314724) in Seatac (lightrail accessible) at 11:30am to send a message to Alaska Airlines CEO Ben Minicucci that they need to do more to protect their workers and passengers from the [violence ICE is inflicting at our airports](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=WvqNUkN05h8$0).

This event is peaceful, and will include a short march from Angle Lake Park to [Alaska Airlines headquarters](https://www.mapquest.com/us/washington/seatac/98188-5304/19300-international-blvd-47.42927,-122.29309$0).

We call on Alaska Airlines CEO Ben Minicucci to condemn the U.S. Immigration and Customs Enforcement (ICE) and implement changes organization-wide to protect our communities, passengers and workers from [ICE brutality at our airports](https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=WvqNUkN05h8$0). This includes:

* __Sending a direct demand__ to the U.S. Department of Homeland Security (DHS) that ICE be removed from all our airports;

* __Demanding judicial warrants__ of ICE agents and more robust training for Alaska Airlines staff on their protocol and rights when ICE interferes with a flight or passengers;

* __Limiting sharing of passenger data__ with ICE;

* __No repercussions for Alaska Airlines staff__ refusing to work when ICE creates safety issues for passengers.

__Our communities have had ENOUGH—tell Alaska Airlines & all airport businesses to stand with their passengers in demanding ICE OUT__
